From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: B Honey <9922368+Mhsbrian@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 08:56:10 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/7] nvk: link with the common Vulkan ICD version script

Unlike RADV, ANV, Turnip, PanVK and v3dv, libvulkan_nouveau is not
linked with vulkan_icd_link_args. gnu_symbol_visibility hides its C
symbols, but every #[no_mangle] function of the Rust parts (NAK, NIL)
and the public items of the Rust standard library are still exported:
on an Android x86_64 build of Mesa 26.2.5, vulkan.nouveau.so exports
2639 dynamic symbols, where vulkan.radv.so exports only HMI.

Those exports can interpose on other copies of the same symbols in a
process that also loads another Mesa driver (for example Zink in
libgallium_dri.so with NVK as its Vulkan driver), and on Android they
are outside the HAL contract, which is HMI alone.

Link with the version script the other drivers use (vulkan.sym, or
vulkan-android.sym on Android) and add the symbols check that RADV and
PanVK run.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/nouveau/vulkan/meson.build | 19 ++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/nouveau/vulkan/meson.build b/src/nouveau/vulkan/meson.build
index f0bb780fb1f..706c7d8463f 100644
--- a/src/nouveau/vulkan/meson.build
+++ b/src/nouveau/vulkan/meson.build
@@ -184,11 +184,28 @@ libnvk = static_library(
 libvulkan_nouveau = shared_library(
   'vulkan_nouveau',
   link_whole : [libnvk],
-  link_args: [ld_args_build_id, ld_args_bsymbolic, ld_args_gc_sections],
+  link_args: [
+    ld_args_build_id, ld_args_bsymbolic, ld_args_gc_sections,
+    vulkan_icd_link_args,
+  ],
+  link_depends : vulkan_icd_link_depends,
   gnu_symbol_visibility : 'hidden',
   install : true,
 )
 
+if with_symbols_check
+  test(
+    'nvk symbols check',
+    symbols_check,
+    args : [
+      '--lib', libvulkan_nouveau,
+      '--symbols-file', vulkan_icd_symbols,
+      symbols_check_args,
+    ],
+    suite : ['nouveau'],
+  )
+endif
+
 icd_file_name = libname_prefix + 'vulkan_nouveau.' + libname_suffix
 
 nouveau_icd = custom_target(
